+
+## Built-in token auth
+
+`ConnectionConfig.tokenAuth` enables first-party admission for every `/api` HTTP request and both WebSocket downlinks. Production config uses `storePath`, pointing at the digest-only file generated by `dsh auth token`; the inline `tokens` form remains a compatibility ingress. Non-browser clients may send `Authorization: Bearer <token>` or `x-dsh-access-token`.
+
+A browser exchanges a token with `POST /api/auth/token` and JSON `{ "token": "..." }`. The response contains an opaque `dsh-session` HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict cookie and redirects with `303`; the access token never enters a URL or cookie. `POST /api/auth/logout` clears the session. The gate reloads the digest store while authenticating sessions, so token revoke invalidates derived sessions without a DSH restart.
+
+An `admin`-scoped token also unlocks the privileged method set that otherwise stays loopback-only (`settings.*`, `credentials.*`, `host.pickDirectory`, `host.openPath`, and the agent-preset authoring methods). This is the authentication layer that makes non-loopback `dsh web` deployments safe to operate.
